  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study Circular Economy, Benin</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to gain insights in the opportunities and barriers for circular use in the agricultural value chains of the Project &quot;Approche communale pour le March&#xE9; Agricole au B&#xE9;nin&quot; (ACMA), by identifying opportunities for reducing and/or reusing waste streams in and among the agricultural value chains of ACMA.Specifically, the project is focused on mapping the sustainable applications for agricultural waste in the ACMA value chains and identifying opportunities to valorise these waste streams.The objective is to carry out a comprehensive analysis of the current waste streams and current uses of these streams and to feasibility study and to identify concrete business cases related to circularity in the agricultural value chains promoted by the ACMA programme.</narrative>
  </description>
